# PlatformIO build output, downloaded platforms/libs, and IDE metadata.
.pio/

# Build-time secrets. ⚠ Kept here rather than deferred to issue #79 with the rest of
# the OTA tooling, because firmware/wifi_secret.ini EXISTS ON DISK NOW: it was written
# during 3.9c planning, and on 2026-08-24 an earlier copy of it reached a public repo
# through the GitHub web UI, which honours no .gitignore. Nothing in this commit reads
# the file yet — `extra_configs` wiring lands with #79 — and the rule still earns its
# place today, because the window where a secret is untracked and unignored is exactly
# the window that already cost us a password rotation.
#
# Deliberately NOT named `.env*`: that namespace is a blanket permission deny fleet-wide
# (DEC-S043), so a secret living there is one no session can read in order to debug it.
*secret*.ini
